// Operation policy matches the existing FFN profile: 0 = qk_compat,
// 1 = canonical. GGUF weight tags select encoding independently of policy.
// Both operations use the same policy and Q8_1 x4 physical row layout.
// Canonical processes every launched row; compatible preserves inactive rows.
// A nonnegative fixed_count bypasses count; negative reads I32 at count_origin.
// Input and weights are read. Packed/output are written only for produced rows.
// Callers supply disjoint storage and retain allocation/reuse ownership.
// launch_rows is a static launch extent; row_capacity is the runtime view extent.
// Origins in the data buffers are supplied through caller-created zero-origin
// views. row_origin/count_origin describe the existing logical activity ABI.
